    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0673" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v01/pg645"/>

                <head>299. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State and
                    the Director of Central Intelligence (McCone)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d299-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1964-08-06T13:10:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 6, 1964, 1:10
                    p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">TELEPHONE CALL FROM MR. McCONE</p>
                <p>Sec said his secure phone was not buttoned up and he would have to talk to M on
                    this one. M said he had gone into the question of the use of some of the
                    sensitive information to prove the night attack <pb facs="0674" n="646"
                        xml:id="pg646"/> and disprove Hanoi’s allegation that it did not take place;
                    it just cannot be used; we will have to have eyewitness accounts and things of
                    that kind.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
